### CORS Configuration (for UI integration)

In each API's Program.cs:

```csharp
builder.Services.AddCors(options =>
{
    options.AddDefaultPolicy(policy =>
    {
        policy.WithOrigins("http://localhost:3000", "http://localhost:4200")
              .AllowAnyHeader()
              .AllowAnyMethod();
    });
});

// In Configure section
app.UseCors();
```

## Running the Services

### Option 1: Run All Services (PowerShell Script)

Create `run-all-services.ps1`:

```powershell
# Run all services in separate windows
Start-Process powershell -ArgumentList "-NoExit", "-Command", "cd src\Services\Compliance\Compliance.API; dotnet run"
Start-Process powershell -ArgumentList "-NoExit", "-Command", "cd src\Services\Allocation\Allocation.API; dotnet run"
Start-Process powershell -ArgumentList "-NoExit", "-Command", "cd src\Services\TradeBooking\TradeBooking.API; dotnet run"
Start-Process powershell -ArgumentList "-NoExit", "-Command", "cd src\Services\TradeOrchestrator\TradeOrchestrator.API; dotnet run"
Start-Process powershell -ArgumentList "-NoExit", "-Command", "cd src\Services\FundData\FundData.API; dotnet run"
Start-Process powershell -ArgumentList "-NoExit", "-Command", "cd src\Services\ReferenceData\ReferenceData.API; dotnet run"
```

Run it:
```powershell
.\run-all-services.ps1
```

### Option 2: Run Individually

Open 6 terminal windows and run each service:

```bash
# Terminal 1
cd src/Services/Compliance/Compliance.API
dotnet run --urls "http://localhost:5001"

# Terminal 2
cd src/Services/Allocation/Allocation.API
dotnet run --urls "http://localhost:5002"

# Terminal 3
cd src/Services/TradeBooking/TradeBooking.API
dotnet run --urls "http://localhost:5003"

# Terminal 4
cd src/Services/TradeOrchestrator/TradeOrchestrator.API
